@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<style>
    .privacy-page {
        background: #f5f8ff;
        color: #27364b;
        padding-bottom: 45px;
    }

    .privacy-hero {
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #12376b, #2874c8);
        color: white;
        padding: 48px 20px;
        text-align: center;
        border-radius: 0 0 25px 25px;
    }

    .privacy-hero h1 {
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.8rem);
        font-weight: 800;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .privacy-hero p {
        max-width: 750px;
        margin: auto;
        color: #edf5ff;
        line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .privacy-container {
        max-width: 1000px;
        margin: auto;
        padding: 32px 18px 0;
    }

    .privacy-card {
        background: white;
        border: 1px solid #e2eaf5;
        border-radius: 15px;
        padding: 25px;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        box-shadow: 0 5px 18px rgba(25, 55, 95, 0.05);
    }

    .privacy-card h2 {
        color: #193f70;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        margin-bottom: 13px;
    }

    .privacy-card p,
    .privacy-card li {
        color: #596a80;
        line-height: 1.8;
        font-size: 0.97rem;
    }

    .privacy-card ul {
        padding-left: 22px;
        margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .privacy-icon {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        margin-right: 8px;
    }

    .privacy-notice {
        background: #eaf3ff;
        border-left: 4px solid #2874c8;
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 20px;
        color: #294b77;
        line-height: 1.8;
        margin-bottom: 25px;
    }

    @@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
        .privacy-hero {
            padding: 38px 16px;
        }

        .privacy-container {
            padding: 22px 13px 0;
        }

        .privacy-card {
            padding: 19px;
        }
    }
</style>

<div class="privacy-page">

    <section class="privacy-hero">
        <div class="container">
            <div style="font-size: 2.7rem;" class="mb-2">🔐</div>
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p>
                Your privacy matters to us. This page explains how information
                may be collected, used, and protected when you use the
                CivicTrace.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="privacy-container">

        <div class="privacy-notice">
            <strong>Important information</strong>
            <p class="mb-0 mt-2">
                This policy describes the intended privacy practices of this
                project. The actual handling of information depends on the
                application's implementation, database configuration, and
                hosting environment.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">📌</span>1. Purpose of the Website</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                The CivicTrace provides an online platform for
                citizens to report public problems, submit supporting
                information, and follow the progress of their complaints.
                Information is used to help authorized officials review
                complaints and manage their resolution.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">🧾</span>2. Information We May Collect</h2>
            <p>The application may process the following information when it is provided or generated through its features:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account information:</strong> Details associated with registration and login, such as email address.</li>
                <li><strong>Complaint information:</strong> Complaint title, description, category, priority, and status.</li>
                <li><strong>Location information:</strong> Coordinates, address, or PIN code associated with a complaint, when provided or enabled.</li>
                <li><strong>Images and evidence:</strong> Photographs uploaded to explain a reported issue.</li>
                <li><strong>Complaint history:</strong> Status changes, timestamps, department assignments, and remarks recorded by the application.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">🎯</span>3. How Information Is Used</h2>
            <p>Information may be used to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Create, store, and manage public complaints.</li>
                <li>Help identify the location of a reported issue.</li>
                <li>Support complaint categorization and priority suggestions.</li>
                <li>Help authorized officials review and process complaints.</li>
                <li>Display complaint status, history, and available updates to the relevant citizen.</li>
                <li>Identify possible duplicate complaints where the feature is enabled.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">👁️</span>4. Who Can Access Complaint Information?</h2>
            <p>
                Citizens should access only their own complaint details through
                the citizen-facing pages. Authorized officials may access
                complaint information needed for their assigned duties,
                according to their roles and permissions.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Users should avoid including passwords, banking details,
                government identification numbers, or other unnecessary
                sensitive information in complaint descriptions or uploaded
                images.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">📍</span>5. Location and Uploaded Images</h2>
            <p>
                Location details help officials understand where a public
                issue occurred. Uploaded images may help explain the problem
                and support complaint review.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Citizens should check photographs before uploading them and
                avoid including faces, private documents, or personal details
                unless they are necessary for reporting the issue.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">🤖</span>6. AI-Assisted Features</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                The system includes AI-assisted components intended to help
                classify complaint descriptions and identify possible
                duplicate complaints. Additional image-analysis capabilities
                depend on the configured implementation. Automated
                suggestions may not always be correct and should be reviewed
                where appropriate.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">🛡️</span>7. Security</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                The application is designed to use authentication and
                role-based access to protect its pages and complaint
                information. Users should keep their passwords private,
                log out when using a shared device, and report suspected
                unauthorized access. No website or storage system can
                guarantee absolute security.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">🗄️</span>8. Data Storage and Retention</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Account details, complaints, uploaded files, and status
                history may be stored by the application to provide its
                services. How long this information is retained and when it
                is deleted depends on the project's actual storage and
                retention settings.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">🔗</span>9. Third-Party Services</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Mapping, hosting, or other external services may process
                information when those integrations are enabled. Their
                handling of data is governed by their own terms and privacy
                policies. Users should review those policies where relevant.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">✏️</span>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                This policy may be updated when the application's features,
                data practices, or security arrangements change. The
                information displayed on this page should be reviewed
                periodically to keep it accurate.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="privacy-card">
            <h2><span class="privacy-icon">📩</span>11. Questions About Privacy</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                If you have questions about information handled by this
                project, contact the website administrator or the
                organization responsible for operating the system.
                Official contact details should be provided by the
                organization when available.
            </p>
        </section>

    </div>
</div>
